address for mapping, defaulting to 1 GB, but choosing 0.5  GB  on
machines with less than 192 MB RAM and 2 GB on machines with more
than 1 GB of RAM.  The intent is to use an address that is larger
than  available RAM, but low enough to work; some systems seem to
have trouble with addresses requiring more than 20 address lines.
